l style=3D"margin-top: 0em; margin-bottom: 0em;"><li style=3D"list-style-ty=
pe: none;" margin-left:=3D"" 6em;=3D""><b>function:</b> DNA-dependent RNA p=
olymerase catalyzes the transcription of DNA into RNA using the four ribonu=
cleoside triphosphates as substrates. This subunit often mutates to generat=
e rifampicin (Rif) resistance. Interaction with RbpA partially restores Rif=
-inhibited transcription; once the subunit is Rif-resistant however RbpA no=
 longer stimulates transcription. <br>
<b>catalytic</b> <b>activity:</b> RNA(n) + a ribonucleoside 5'-triphosphate=
 =3D RNA(n+1) + diphosphate <small>(<a href=3D"https://www.rhea-db.org/reac=
tion?id=3D21248">RHEA:21248</a>)</small><br>
<b>subunit:</b> The RNAP catalytic core consists of 2 alpha, 1 beta, 1 beta=
' and 1 omega subunit (PubMed:19926651, PubMed:33339823). When a sigma fact=
or is associated with the core the holoenzyme is formed, which can initiate=
 transcription. Interacts with RbpA, which partially restores Rif-inhibited=
 transcription (PubMed:19926651). RNAP, HelR, RbpA, promoter DNA and sigma =
factors SigA or SigB can all exist in one complex (PubMed:33339823, PubMed:=
39384756). HelR interacts directly with the beta and beta' subunits (PubMed=
:33339823, PubMed:39384756). </li><li style=3D"list-style-type: none;" marg=
